status: low-latency binary TCP ESP streaming candidate
previous_version: 0_3_5
passed_baseline: 0_2_4
notes: V036 replaces the ESP-to-PC HTTP/MJPEG hot path with one PC-initiated persistent length-prefixed TCP JPEG stream while retaining HTTP only for control/status and retaining the existing PC-to-browser MJPEG relay. The ESP sends a fixed 16-byte ATL1 header plus each JPEG, uses TCP_NODELAY/keepalive, CAMERA_GRAB_LATEST with two PSRAM framebuffers, deadline-based FPS scheduling, and a bounded per-frame send deadline that drops a congested connection rather than accumulating stale visual backlog. PC Studio performs exact fixed-length reads, validates sequence/size/JPEG boundaries, automatically restores lost ESP sessions, and rejects mismatched pre-V036 firmware before opening the binary stream. The tracked PlatformIO firmware is rewritten from the legacy per-frame HTTP POST uploader to match the active PC-controlled architecture, and a standalone Arduino IDE sketch is included. Simulation, Live AI, Dataset Capture, zones and analytics continue to use the shared PC frame service. V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline until explicit owner acceptance changes it. Physical/public-road signal control remains disabled.
